  "id": "medic-open-daybed",
  "name": "His drawing, with the stacked bunks across the stern",
  "idea": "Drawn from the marks of the game's maker on the earlier plan \"Engineering and quarters side by side\". The starboard airlock and the supply store are one pharmacy and lab area, open to the crew hall with no wall or door: one big room, with an island counter for the lab's gear. One airlock, on the port side, with the washroom beside it. Both ramps open into the med bay, and with both down you see straight through the ship. There is no aft corridor: its wall is gone and the crew's quarters are one room, with a small kitchen and a table in what was the corridor's rear. Engineering keeps its wall and its door. Every bed is a normal single. Here the 2-high bunk lies across the stern and the third bunk is a low day bed along the hull, a settee by day, so the crew room is open at head height from the door to the kitchen. The pharmacy and lab are as in his drawing.",
